The purpose is not fear.
The purpose is readiness.
 
Chapter Conclusion
Economic uncertainty is not a modern phenomenon.
Every generation faces periods of abundance and periods of difficulty.
What distinguishes resilient individuals from vulnerable ones is rarely luck.
It is preparation.
The prophetic model teaches that prosperity should never be consumed entirely in the present.
Part of today's abundance belongs to tomorrow's responsibilities.
Saving, when practiced with wisdom and balance, is not an expression of fear.
It is an expression of stewardship.
And stewardship transforms uncertainty from a source of anxiety into an opportunity for preparation.
This is the essence of sustainable prosperity.
Not merely having resources.
But having the foresight, discipline, and perspective to preserve them before they are needed.
