Wealth Was Never Meant to Stand Still
One of the recurring themes throughout Islamic economic thought is that wealth is not an end in itself.
It is a tool.
A trust.
A resource entrusted to human beings for responsible use.
Resources that cease serving a purpose eventually lose their value.
Knowledge that is never shared diminishes.
Talents that are never used deteriorate.
Relationships that are never nurtured weaken.
Wealth follows a similar pattern.
Its purpose is not merely possession.
