They may constantly worry about future shortages.
They may hesitate to help others despite possessing more than enough.
Behavioral psychologists often describe this phenomenon as scarcity thinking.
Scarcity thinking convinces individuals that there will never be enough.
No amount feels sufficient.
No milestone feels secure.
No achievement creates lasting peace.
The problem is not the size of the bank account.
The problem is the mindset governing it.
Fear creates attachment.
Attachment creates anxiety.
Anxiety creates paralysis.
Generosity interrupts this cycle.
Every act of giving challenges the belief that survival depends entirely upon accumulation.
