Their emotions fluctuate with markets.
Their sense of worth becomes linked to financial outcomes.
Generosity breaks this dependency.
It reminds the individual that money is a servant, not a master.
A tool, not an identity.
A resource, not a source of ultimate security.
This shift creates an extraordinary form of freedom.
